    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Left lateral ankle sprain (S93.402A)</content>. Inversion sprain of the anterior talofibular ligament, grade 1 to 2. No X-ray is needed by the Ottawa ankle rules. The fall came from left foot drop on a day he did not wear the orthosis. [S]<list><item>Lace-up ankle brace, ice, elevation, and early protected walking.</item><item>Ibuprofen 400 mg every 8 hours with food as needed for up to 5 days.</item><item>Physical therapy for ankle range of motion and balance.</item><item>Wear the ankle-foot orthosis for all walking outside the house once the swelling allows.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (G12.21)</content>. No change in strength. Two-month ALT on riluzole drawn today: 41 U/L, normal. The fall is an expected risk of foot drop and is shared with the ALS clinic team. [S]<list><item>Continue riluzole.</item><item>Home safety review by occupational therapy.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Practice parameter update: the care of the patient with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis: drug, nutritional, and respiratory therapies (an evidence-based review) (2009); Practice parameter update: the care of the patient with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis: multidisciplinary care, symptom management, and cognitive/behavioral impairment (an evidence-based review) (2009); Ankle Stability and Movement Coordination Impairments: Lateral Ankle Ligament Sprains Revision 2021 (2021)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Phone check in one week. ALS clinic and primary care visit in about five weeks, or sooner for worse pain or inability to bear weight. Next scheduled visit 2026-08-24: three months after diagnosis: ALSFRS-R, breathing, weight, speech, mobility equipment, and work accommodations. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
